      "message": "This is used in a lot of places. One example: before a buffer is used in a command buffer, whenever it\u0027s used in a copy command, etc, `buffer-\u003eNeedsInitialized` is called. `NeedsInitialized` in turn checks for a toggle.\n\nThis change basically turns a simple bit test into multiple ifs and jumps. Are we OK with this? It might prevent inline and other compiler optimizations.",
